# Project Engineering Standards

- Communicate with the user in Russian by default. Keep explanations educational and honest about trade-offs.
- Work incrementally. Inspect existing code first and follow local architecture instead of rewriting broadly.
- Keep FastAPI entrypoints thin. Put business logic and orchestration into dedicated services under `backend/app/services/`.
- Treat RAG evidence strictly: retrieved sources are evidence; memory and summaries are context, not evidence.
- Enforce access boundaries in backend filters before prompt construction. The LLM must never decide what the user can see.
- Preserve traceability for document ingestion: `tenant_id`, `bucket_id`, `document_id`, `source_type`, `source_path`, and meaningful `document_metadata`.
- Prefer multiple explicit evidence layers over one generic blob: text, rows, OCR, vision digest, chart evidence, and consistency evidence can coexist for the same file.
- Add focused unit tests for meaningful logic and evaluation scenarios for user-visible RAG behavior.
- Do not weaken failed evaluations blindly. First diagnose retrieval, chunking, metadata, prompt, evaluator, or model behavior.
- Use stronger evaluators where needed: marker groups, numeric normalization, source metadata flags, and no-leak checks.
- Update `backend/README.md`, `research/LESSONS_LEARNED.md`, `research/RAG_EVALUATION_CHECKLIST.md`, and relevant plans after completed milestones.
- Commit only when the user explicitly asks. Do not commit personal/local raw files unless explicitly approved.
- Document future hardening instead of adding heavy infrastructure prematurely.
